{
 "about": "Exact reference values for popcorn.twosfs at n = 3..6. Each row is a Lambda-coalescent (Beta(2-alpha, alpha) with param = alpha, or Dirac with param = psi; constant size) whose normalized expected 1-SFS xi_hat lies exactly in the convex hull of the normalized single-time Kingman moments m1(t) at the rational levels support_t with the exact convex weights sfs_mixture_weights (an explicit certificate that the 1-SFS is reproduced by a pooled variable-size Kingman history, in the closure sense: atoms are limit histories). Q_lambda is the exact normalized 2-SFS q_ij = E[L_i L_j]/E[L_tot^2] (keys 'i,j', i <= j). proj_* and dist2_sq_exact are the exact Euclidean projection of Q_lambda onto the hull of the normalized atom second moments m2(t), t in support_t (twosfs_hull.project_hull: active set as indices into support_t, exact weights, exact squared distance in the multiplicity-weighted Frobenius norm); delta_l1_lb_exact = dist2_sq / max|w_ij| is the implied lower bound on the l1 distance over ordered pairs. dist2_sq > 0 in every row: no pooling of atom histories on the 1-SFS certificate's own support reproduces the 2-SFS. The kingman row is the scoping control: the constant-size Kingman coalescent's 1-SFS is such a mixture too (support 0, 373/512, 1) yet its 2-SFS is outside that finite-support hull, so this register says nothing about time-varying histories (see class_certificates.json for the class-wide certificates). within_lambda_n3 records that at n = 3 Beta(alpha = 1/2) and Dirac(psi = 3/4) share both the exact 1-SFS (5/6, 1/6) and the exact 2-SFS. All values are outputs of the exact engine (fractions as num/den strings), not data.",
